    {
      "title": "Build Secure SoCs From The Start",
      "date": "2026-09-23",
      "source": "SemiEngineering",
      "url": "https://semiengineering.com/build-secure-socs-from-the-start/",
      "summary": "Practical guide to hardware security assurance in modern semiconductor design. The post Build Secure SoCs From The Start appeared first on Semiconductor Engineering.",
      "body": "Modern semiconductor systems have reached unprecedented levels of complexity.\n\nToday’s system-on-chip (SoC) architectures integrate hundreds of heterogeneous IP blocks, multiple compute engines, shared memory hierarchies, and extensive firmware and software stacks.\n\nWhile these capabilities enable powerful computing platforms, including AI and machine learning, they also expand the hardware attack surface deep into the silicon architecture.\n\nWith this eBook, you will learn how to:\n\nDetect vulnerabilities early in the development lifecycle.\n\nReduce costly silicon respins.\n\nDeliver secure silicon products with greater confidence.\n\nRead more here.\n\nThe post Build Secure SoCs From The Start appeared first on Semiconductor Engineering.",
